 [1/4] Found: CMake suite maintained and supported by Kitware (kitware.com/cmake).
 [X] No C++ compiler was found.

 FIX - pick ONE:
   A. Visual Studio 2022 Community (recommended on Windows):
        winget install Microsoft.VisualStudio.2022.Community --silent --override "--add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Workload.NativeDesktop --includeRecommended --passive"
      Or download from: https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/
      (tick "Desktop development with C++" during install)

   B. MSYS2 UCRT64 (lightweight, no Visual Studio):
        winget install MSYS2.MSYS2
      Then in the UCRT64 terminal run:
        pacman -S --needed mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-cmake mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-make

 Then double-click Build.bat again.

